---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Cube from '../components/Cube.astro';
import symbolLight from '../../brand/web/symbol-color.svg';
import symbolDark from '../../brand/web/symbol-dark.svg';
import {
  DOC,
  REPO_URL,
  ORG_URL,
  CONTACT_EMAIL,
  BUILDER_NAME,
  BUILDER_URL,
  RELEASE_TAG,
  RELEASE_URL,
  CHANGELOG_URL,
} from '../consts';

const title = 'About | MetricMine';
const description =
  'About MetricMine: a contract-driven data pipeline built in the open as a reference implementation, its origin, its name and mark, its decision register, and how to reach the project.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/about/">
  <PageHero eyebrow="About" title="A reference implementation, kept honest in public.">
    MetricMine is a contract-driven medallion pipeline that runs end to end
    on one machine, built in the open so that every claim it makes can be
    checked by someone who has never talked to its author.
  </PageHero>

  <section>
    <div class="container split">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">The project</p>
        <h2>What it is, in one paragraph.</h2>
        <p>
          Raw data lands in bronze exactly as received. A deterministic profiler
          describes it. Machine-readable ODCS contracts, hand-written or drafted
          by two narrow AI agents, shape silver and gold behind a human approval
          gate. An auto-modeling engine emits the entire gold layer from the
          approved contracts, and a read-only MCP server serves the result with
          a context registry one join from any payload, so an assistant answers
          business questions grounded in both the data and the meaning behind
          it. The current tagged release is{' '}
          <a href={RELEASE_URL}>{RELEASE_TAG}</a>; the{' '}
          <a href={CHANGELOG_URL}>changelog</a> records what each release
          landed.
        </p>
        <p class="eyebrow">Origin</p>
        <h2>2023, then 2026 in the open.</h2>
        <p>
          MetricMine began as a private prototype in 2023. The current codebase
          was rebuilt in the open in 2026 from a written specification, with
          the clean-room rule recorded in <a href={DOC.notice}>NOTICE</a>: the
          repository was built fresh from an independent written
          specification, and no code from the 2023 prototype was read,
          imported, or adapted.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">The name and the mark</p>
        <h2>MetricMine. One word, capital M twice.</h2>
        <div class="mark-row">
          <img class="symbol-light" src={symbolLight.src} width="72" height="72" alt="The MetricMine symbol: three connected isometric cubes" />
          <img class="symbol-dark" src={symbolDark.src} width="72" height="72" alt="" />
          <p>
            The symbol is three connected cubes. The cubes stand for data
            modeled as cubes; the connections stand for sources joined into
            one star, which is what the engine builds.
          </p>
        </div>
        <p>
          The name and the logo are not covered by the Apache-2.0 license.
          Forks and derivative works may not use them in a way that suggests
          endorsement by, or affiliation with, this project. The brand system,
          with its vector masters and the normative standard, lives in{' '}
          <a href={DOC.websiteRepo}>the website repository</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it is kept</p>
        <h2>The register is the project's memory.</h2>
        <p>
          Every design judgment is a numbered decision in a versioned
          register, minted by its own documentation pull request before any
          implementing change lands. Every measurement that contradicted a
          plan is a numbered finding. The stable line changes only through
          that machinery.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cards">
        <article class="card">
          <Cube />
          <h3>Forty-one decisions.</h3>
          <p>
            D-01 through D-41 with their amendments, each condensed in full
            operational substance, and a crosswalk to the rule each one became
            in the coding agent's instructions.
          </p>
          <span class="under"><a href={DOC.register}>docs/decisions/decision-register.md</a></span>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <Cube />
          <h3>Fifty-three findings.</h3>
          <p>
            F-01 through F-53: toolchain behavior observed live, never
            inferred, from the first scratch gate proof to the multi-source
            trial, each one with the evidence it cites.
          </p>
          <span class="under"><a href={DOC.findings}>docs/verification/gate_proof_findings.md</a></span>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <Cube />
          <h3>One stability rule.</h3>
          <p>
            From v1.0.0, the pipeline, the engine, the serving layer, the two
            proposers, and the gates change only through the register, and a
            clone of main at any tag gets a working demo.
          </p>
          <span class="under"><a href={DOC.claudeMd}>CLAUDE.md, rule 19</a></span>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container split">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">Who</p>
        <h2>Built by {BUILDER_NAME}.</h2>
        <p>
          MetricMine is a personal open source project, built and maintained
          on its author's own time. The commits, the pull requests, and the
          register carry the record; the profile is{' '}
          <a href={BUILDER_URL}>{BUILDER_NAME} on GitHub</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
        <h2>One address, one organization.</h2>
        <p>
          Questions, findings, and pull requests belong on{' '}
          <a href={REPO_URL}>the repository</a>. Anything else reaches the
          project at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
          The GitHub organization is <a href={ORG_URL}>metricminellc</a>, a
          namespace and nothing more.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .band {
      background: var(--mm-bg-raised);
      border-block: 1px solid var(--mm-border);
    }

    .mark-row {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 72px minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 18px;
      align-items: start;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
    }

    .mark-row img {
      width: 72px;
      height: 72px;
    }

    .mark-row p {
      margin: 0;
    }

    .symbol-dark {
      display: none;
    }

    :global([data-theme='dark']) .symbol-dark {
      display: block;
    }

    :global([data-theme='dark']) .symbol-light {
      display: none;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
